From 482ad48fdbf8a293999ed1b8ceebad5293dfc790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kewen Lin <linkewen@hygon.cn>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:34:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] i386: Add -mveclibabi=hvml for HYGON vector math library

GCC supports generating vectorized math calls to Intel SVML and the
AMD ACML and AOCL libraries.  Add equivalent support for the HYGON
vector math library (HVML) through -mveclibabi=hvml.

The new handler maps 32 scalar math function families to the HVML
entry-point naming convention.  Record the selected single- and double-precision
vector widths alongside their operation cases, and translate the log
operation to the HVML ln spelling.  The handler requires a 64-bit target
and unsafe math optimizations.  See invoke.texi for the complete list of
mapped functions.

The GCC 16 backport omits the seven C23 pi-based trigonometric
families because this branch lacks their type-specific builtin lookup
mappings. Remove the corresponding HVML documentation and test
expectations.

Add three testcases.  The first checks all 166 selected operation,
precision, and vector-width combinations independently using
-march=c86-4g-m7 and -mprefer-vector-width=512.  The others check that
HVML calls are disabled without unsafe math optimizations and that
-mno-avx selects only 128-bit HVML calls.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* config/i386/i386-options.cc (ix86_option_override_internal):
	Handle ix86_veclibabi_type_hvml case.
	* config/i386/i386-options.h (ix86_veclibabi_hvml): New declare.
	* config/i386/i386-opts.h (enum ix86_veclibabi): Add
	ix86_veclibabi_type_hvml into the ix86_veclibabi enum.
	* config/i386/i386.cc (ix86_veclibabi_hvml): New function.
	* config/i386/i386.opt: Add the hvml type.
	* doc/invoke.texi: Document -mveclibabi=hvml and clarify the 64-bit
	restriction for ACML and AOCL.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/i386/vectorize-hvml-1.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/i386/vectorize-hvml-2.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/i386/vectorize-hvml-3.c: Likewise.

